/* Measured 2026-08-04, Chromium, 390px viewport, the six controls a host actually sees (mic, camera,
   screen, hand, leave, end):

     button 62px (the phone floor below) vs label «Выключить микрофон» 116.7px  -> ±27.3px spill
     button 62px vs «Завершить для всех» 107.5px                                -> ±22.7px spill
     five of six labels spilled; neighbouring captions overlapped into unreadable text

   Cause: the strip is a flex row, so every control shrinks to its `min-width` floor as soon as the row
   does not fit — which on a phone is always. The caption is `nowrap` with no overflow control, so it
   kept its full width and painted over the adjacent buttons instead of being contained.

   The strip is already `overflow-x: auto`, i.e. scrolling — not shrinking — was the intended answer to
   a row that does not fit. `flex: 0 0 auto` restores that: a control is at least its floor and never
   narrower than its own caption. The `span` rule stays as a contained fallback for any future label
   long enough to exceed its own button. Content 507px in a 370px strip, 0 of 6 spilling. */
.gc-conference-controls .gc-conference-control { flex: 0 0 auto; }
.gc-conference-control span { max-width: 100%; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
